"""
hedging_effectiveness.py
========================
Farm-level hedging effectiveness for French winter wheat.
Per-hectare revenue, OOS 2016-2024, 8 NUTS-2 regions.

Design
------
  1. Additive yield detrending (Möllmann et al. 2019):
       Y_t^detrend = Y_t - Y_hat_t^trend + Y_bar
     where Y_hat_t^trend = alpha + beta*t fitted on calibration data.

  2. Contract (index type, accumulation window) selected ONCE per region
     using all data prior to the OOS period (< 2019) by maximising
     |Pearson r| between detrended yield and accumulated index.
     The same contract is held fixed across all 6 OOS years.

  3. Yield model: fixed quadratic levels specification per Vedenov &
     Barnett (2004) and Zhou et al. (2016):
       Y_t^detrend = a + b*I_t + c*I_t^2 + eps_t,  eps ~ N(0, sigma^2)
     No AIC model selection -- quadratic form used throughout.

  4. Strike K* (Möllmann et al. 2019 / Conradt et al. 2015):
       Solve yield model for I = K* such that a + b*K* + c*K*² = Y_bar.
     Grounds the contract in the insured variable rather than the raw
     index distribution. Quadratic formula; falls back to historical mean
     if no real root lies within a 3-sigma band of the index.

  5. Johnson (1960) / Ederington (1979) OLS minimum-variance hedge ratio:
       N* = -Cov(R_u, payoff) / Var(payoff),  floored at 0.

  6. Common historical burn premium -- model-independent:
       V = exp(-r*T) * mean(realised payoffs over calibration years).
     Premium is computed at K* so it is consistent with the contract.

  7. Ex-post evaluation on detrended actual yield (same scale as simulation).

Primary statistic: DeltaRev = R_h - R_u (EUR/ha).
Significance: two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank (primary) + t-test.
Secondary: HE_var, HE_sv.

References
----------
  Vedenov & Barnett (2004); Zhou et al. (2016); Möllmann et al. (2019);
  Conradt et al. (2015); Ederington (1979); Johnson (1960);
  Pelka & Musshoff (2013/2014).
"""

