# Hedge-ratio policy: direct semivariance minimisation, capped at
# N* <= 1 contract per hectare ("textbook full hedge" ceiling).
#
# For each (model, region, OOS year), N* is found by 1D numerical search:
#     N* = argmin_{0 <= N <= N_STAR_CAP}
#                 mean( min(R_h_sim - mean(R_u_sim), 0)^2 )
# where R_h_sim = R_u_sim - N * V * exp(r*T) + N * P_sim.
#
# Why SV (not Var) and why a hard cap:
#   - SV directly targets downside-revenue protection (the asymmetric
#     metric a risk-averse hedger actually cares about), so unlike
#     Johnson's variance-minimising OLS it does not explode when the
#     model's bootstrap distribution is sharp (the "1/sigma_P" pathology).
#   - The cap at 1 contract/ha eliminates the few cells where the
#     unconstrained SV optimisation still recommends economically
#     implausible positions (LSTM's max N* of 12.4 in the uncapped
#     version), preserving forecast-quality differences without letting
#     two outlier cells dominate the realised variance.
N_STAR_CAP = 1.0

